; gRPC over the same Mirage_flow.S the HTTP client uses.
;
; Deliberately h2-lwt and not h2-mirage. h2-mirage would do the functorising
; for us, but its closure is 48 packages -- conduit-mirage, tcpip, tls, x509,
; dns-client, vchan, xenstore -- because it assumes a full network stack. The
; confidential Solo5 targets have no such stack; they have a vsock. What h2
; actually needs from a transport is Gluten_lwt.IO, which is four functions,
; so Io_of_flow implements those over a flow and the cone stays small.
;
; The consequence is that gRPC reaches the same places HTTP does, rather than
; being a Unix-only afterthought.

(library
 (name tron_rpc_grpc)
 (public_name tron-rpc-grpc)
 (libraries
  tron-types
  tron-transaction
  tron-proto
  tron-rpc
  web3-codec-protobuf
  grpc
  grpc-lwt
  h2
  h2-lwt
  gluten-lwt
  faraday
  bigstringaf
  lwt
  cstruct
  mirage-flow
  fmt))
